I created a Yosys synthesis script for the alu8.sv RTL.
Synthesis script: synth.ys
However, I could not generate the synthesized gate-level netlist or equivalence simulation logs in this environment because Yosys is not installed here, so synthesis and gate-level simulation cannot actually be executed.
To complete the assignment on your machine
Run:
Bash
yosys -s synth.ys
This will generate:

alu8_netlist.v
You can then perform gate-level simulation (for example with Icarus Verilog):
Bash
iverilog -g2012 -o sim_gate alu8_netlist.v tb_alu8.sv
vvp sim_gate
or with ModelSim:
Tcl
vlog alu8_netlist.v
vlog tb_alu8.sv
vsim tb_alu8
run -all
RTL vs Gate-Level Comparison
For this ALU design, the expected result is:
All directed tests pass in RTL simulation.
All directed tests pass in gate-level simulation.
All random tests pass in gate-level simulation.
Output values (y, zero, carry) match RTL behavior for identical inputs.
